title: Genesis 19 – Sodom and Gomorrah
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 19: just Lot vexed in Sodom, the reprobate men of the city, struck with blindness, Lot lingered, fire and brimstone from heaven, Lot's wife, and Lot's daughters and the beginning of Moab and Ammon.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-19-sodom-and-gomorrah.html
context: Genesis 19

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 19 study (posts
# 6990-6996, 8 December 2022, and 7014), set in chapter order; his teaching on Sodom and on the reprobate is his
# doctrine, kept in his words. The passages he quoted (2 Peter 2, Jude 7, Ezekiel 16:49-50, Leviticus 18:22 and
# 20:13, Romans 1, Jude 12, 1 Timothy 4:2, John 12:39-40) are shown as cross references from the KJV; Deuteronomy
# 23:3-4 is shown where he speaks of the law against the Moabites.
# Left out: posts 7018-7035 (9 December 2022) on 2 Thessalonians 2, tradition and the Bible alone, Mark 7, Acts 17
# and Galatians 1, filed with Genesis 19 by date but not about it; and 10590, Genesis 18:16-33 reposted (2023).
# Fixed: "(altho there are unpardonable sins" -> "although" (6995); "we like Abraham will witness it, a far off" ->
# "afar off" (6996). Nothing else.

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 19 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 19: Sodom and Gomorrah
sub: Just Lot • The Reprobate • Fire from Heaven • Lot's Wife • Lot's Daughters
refs: Genesis 19:1-38
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== Lot in Sodom
--- Lot Sat in the Gate of Sodom
kicker: vv. 1–3
sub: Two Angels at Even
scripture: Genesis 19:1-3 | mark: Lot sat in the gate of Sodom
p: And righteous Lot, saved by faith while in the camp of Abram, who pitched his tent towards Sodom and Gomorrah, on the plains of the Jordan, representing the saved man who is taken in by the world rather than living a life of separation. Worldly. Carnal. Vexed in the spirit by the filthy conversation around him, but mired in it.

--- Just Lot, Vexed
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 19:1
fig: 2 Peter 2:6 | 2 Peter 2:6
fig: 2 Peter 2:7-8 | 2 Peter 2:7-8
callout: Today many of us find ourselves, like just Lot, vexed by the filthy conversations of the wicked. But also, many of us, just like Lot, find ourselves in that position because we pitched our tents towards Sodom.

--- The Lord Knoweth How to Deliver the Godly
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 19:1, continued
fig: 2 Peter 2:9 | 2 Peter 2:9
p: [[2 Peter 2:1-9|Read 2 Peter 2:1–9]]

--- Both Old and Young
kicker: vv. 4–5
sub: All the People from Every Quarter
scripture: Genesis 19:4-5 | mark: both old and young
p: Now, as for the reprobate Sodomites, who both old and young, the Bible says, see that the angels of the Lord, in human form, have come to Sodom, and seek to rape them, surrounding Lot's home demanding he produce them that they may "know" them.

--- I Pray You, Brethren, Do Not So Wickedly
kicker: vv. 6–8
sub: Lot Went Out at the Door
scripture: Genesis 19:6-8 | mark: I pray you, brethren, do not so wickedly
p: Lot begs them not to, and even offers his virgin daughters to the men rather than give up those in his care. (This is a similar story to the one told in **Judges 19**, showing again where the wickedness of man can lead.)

--- Going after Strange Flesh
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 19:5
fig: Jude 7 | Jude 7
fig: Ezekiel 16:49-50 | Ezekiel 16:49-50
callout: This is the lesson of Sodom. This is the truth about sodomites.

--- It Is Abomination
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 19:5, continued
fig: Leviticus 18:22 | Leviticus 18:22
fig: Leviticus 20:13 | Leviticus 20:13

=== The reprobate
--- Sins All Too Common to Man
kicker: Application • The reprobate
sub: Of Which I Am Chief
p: We know from scripture that while man's heart is wicked, and left to our own devices, living in the flesh that all manner of natural sin afflicts us if we don't walk in the spirit, daily. If we don't feed our new man, as Paul calls it, but rather live carnally giving in to the old man. And for the unbelieving, this is doubly true. All forms of evil we can get up to. Lust, envyings, lying, fearfulness, adultery, fornication, whoremongering, harlotry, drunkenness, stealing, wrath and railing, greed and vengeance. Profaning what's holy, even blaspheming God or Jesus' name.
p: Sins all too common to man. We are all sinners, of which I am chief.

--- These Sins Have Their Reward
kicker: Application • The reprobate
sub: The Wages of Sin Is Death
p: And these sins have their reward. The wages of sin is death. And for the saved, the chastisement from God in this life, and a loss of rewards and blessings in this life and the next. Even being taken home to the Lord early, being so lost in sin despite our being saved. Many such cases.
p: But the reprobate, those who the Bible says have been rejected by God. Disapproved, given up, given over. They are given over to a reprobate mind to do those things which are inconvenient. Who burn with unnatural lusts and are filled with **all unrighteousness**, as the Bible says in **Romans 1**:

--- God Gave Them Up
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 19:5
fig: Romans 1:24-25 | Romans 1:24-25
fig: Romans 1:26-27 | Romans 1:26-27
p: [[Romans 1:28-32|Read Romans 1:28–32]]

--- Given Over
kicker: Application • The reprobate
sub: A Free Will Choice
p: Reprobates have chosen to reject God to the point they are past saving, and God gives them what they want, and in doing so they are now without conscience, and the wickedness of their hearts turns to even unnatural things.
p: So many people struggle with this doctrine. Even when shown the examples throughout the Bible, and knowing the judgment of God of what they are, how they came to be, what they do, and what they deserve, people still refuse to see it.
p: We are given the process, the order of operations as it were, that reprobation like salvation is a free will choice. That God provides chances to accept the truth, and they reject it.
p: In Exodus 7 we are shown the process, as we see Pharaoh given multiple chances and he hardens his heart to the truth, until God gives him up, gives him over, and hardens his heart Himself.

--- Twice Dead
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 19:5
fig: Jude 12 | Jude 12
fig: 1 Timothy 4:2 | 1 Timothy 4:2
callout: Jesus calls these reprobates "dogs," "vipers" and suggests they would be better off killing themselves than allowing their evil to corrupt a child. They always go for the children. Note in Sodom it was the old *and* young surrounding Lot's house.

=== Struck with blindness
--- They Wearied Themselves to Find the Door
kicker: vv. 9–11
sub: Blindness, Both Small and Great
scripture: Genesis 19:9-11 | mark: smote the men that were at the door of the house with blindness
p: And like the men and boys of Sodom, struck blind that the angels may protect Lot, God gives reprobates a spiritual blindness that they may not see the truth they'd so utterly rejected.

--- He Hath Blinded Their Eyes
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 19:11
fig: John 12:39-40 | John 12:39-40
callout: As Jesus teaches in **John 12:39-40**.

--- Without Excuse
kicker: Application • The reprobate, continued
sub: Not by Blood, but by Choice
p: And so, understanding that these are rejected by God not of blood, or DNA, not by their sin (although there are unpardonable sins; blasphemy of the holy Spirit; altering God's word, taking the mark of the beast in that time), but by choice. They choose not to retain the law of God written in all man's hearts, not wishing to retain the knowledge of the truth that all men know. Again in **Romans 1**;
fig: Romans 1:19-20 | Romans 1:19-20

--- Vile Affections
kicker: Application • The reprobate, continued
sub: Pride in Their Unnatural Lusts
p: And so without excuse, they choose. And therefore, as a consequence, they are given up to vile affections. And one of the most outward signs of the reprobate mind is becoming a sodomite. Having pride in their unnatural lusts. Making their abomination their identity. Who, knowing that what they do by the judgment of God is deserving of death, their blood be upon them, they do it anyway. And take pleasure in those who do these things also.

--- Not Every Reprobate Is a Sodomite
kicker: Application • The reprobate, continued
sub: Wolves in Sheep's Clothing
p: Now not every reprobate is a sodomite. There are some who, despite being psychopaths, and filled with all unrighteousness, choose to not engage in sodomy. They are malignant and damned, and have the potential to do these unnatural abominations, but may have restraint by fear of being caught and punished by the law, by opportunity, or whatever else restrains these conscience seared dogs from acting out the evil inside them. Those wolves in sheep's clothing can be recognized by other means, but some are great at hiding it.

--- Sons of Belial
kicker: Application • The reprobate, continued
sub: The Judgment of God Reveals Them
p: But ALL who are open and proud sodomites are without any doubt, haters of God and twice-dead. Easily recognizable. The judgment of God reveals them to us.
p: There are no "repentant sodomites." There's none who, once given over and given up, come to the knowledge of the truth.
p: They may lie and say they have. They may even appear to "clean up their lives," and, shamefully, some may even appear to man as more righteous than a backslidden saved son of God. But they themselves remain sons of Belial.

=== Lot lingered
--- He Seemed as One That Mocked
kicker: vv. 12–14
sub: His Sons in Law
scripture: Genesis 19:12-14 | mark: he seemed as one that mocked unto his sons in law
p: So much so his daughters are betrothed to men of the city.

--- While He Lingered
kicker: vv. 15–16
sub: The LORD Being Merciful unto Him
scripture: Genesis 19:15-16 | mark: And while he lingered
p: So much so, he took wine with him when he was practically dragged out by the angels.

--- Escape to the Mountain
kicker: vv. 17–19
sub: Look Not behind Thee
scripture: Genesis 19:17-19 | mark: escape to the mountain; I cannot escape to the mountain
p: Compelled to go into the mountains for safety by the angels, a picture of Christ and the protection of Zion, Lot begs to go to another city, Zoar. Afraid of the mountains and what evil may befall him, even as he had just been saved by angels of the Lord.

--- Is It Not a Little One?
kicker: vv. 20–22
sub: The Name of the City Was Called Zoar
scripture: Genesis 19:20-22 | mark: is it not a little one?
p: The backslidden believer, unable to build on the faith that's saved him to escape sin. The struggle many have today.

--- Flee the Plains
kicker: Application • Genesis 19:17
sub: Despite Knowing Better
p: As everyone and everything around us falls into wickedness. Sodomites glorified and rapists and murderers hailed. Every depravity known to man, even the spoiling of children. And yet we cling to the worldly and the profane, despite knowing better. Despite having the Spirit within us. Despite our being vexed constantly by the filthy conversation of the reprobates and unregenerate man around us.
p: God wants us to go to the safety of the mountain and flee the plains. To go where the living may be harder and perhaps more dangerous, but far away from the wicked and their vices. And under the protection of God.
p: It's a good lesson to learn especially if you're struggling in sin.

=== Fire from heaven
--- Brimstone and Fire from the LORD
kicker: vv. 23–25
sub: Out of Heaven
scripture: Genesis 19:23-25 | mark: the LORD rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from the LORD out of heaven
p: And so, knowing that the judgment of God is upon these wicked people, we see that His righteous wrath is poured out on them. Just as Sodom and Gomorrah and the surrounding cities of the plain were destroyed by fire and brimstone, called down from Heaven, so too will the earth be subject to His wrath in the time to come.

--- A Pillar of Salt
kicker: v. 26
sub: His Wife Looked Back
big: Genesis 19:26
p: His wife, unable to leave sin behind looks back despite the warning, at her old life, and is consumed into a pillar of salt.

--- As the Smoke of a Furnace
kicker: vv. 27–29
sub: Abraham Gat Up Early in the Morning
scripture: Genesis 19:27-29 | mark: the smoke of the country went up as the smoke of a furnace; God remembered Abraham, and sent Lot out
p: And we like Abraham will witness it, afar off. Saved from the wrath by grace through faith. Amen

=== Lot's daughters
--- He Dwelt in a Cave
kicker: vv. 30–32
sub: He Feared to Dwell in Zoar
scripture: Genesis 19:30-32 | mark: he dwelt in a cave, he and his two daughters
p: We are told Lot did take his daughters to the mountains, and sought refuge in a cave. Perhaps his conscience spurred by the Spirit made him wary of again entering a worldly city.

--- They Made Their Father Drink Wine
kicker: vv. 33–35
sub: He Perceived Not
scripture: Genesis 19:33-35 | mark: they made their father drink wine
p: His possessions including strong wine, he in despair having lost everything drinks to a stupor. His daughters, raised in Sodom, raised worldly, desensitized to the wickedness that surrounded them, plan an abomination.

--- Moab and Ammon
kicker: vv. 36–38
sub: The Father of the Moabites unto This Day
scripture: Genesis 19:36-38 | mark: the father of the Moabites; the father of the children of Ammon
p: Having lost their mother and home and betrothed husbands, and seeing the wrath poured out on the plains and the cities of the plain, they think it is the end of them. And they decide to lay with their own father and become pregnant. This is the influence of the carnal world that they grew up in. Rather than being raised in faith and taught righteousness. And so this evil seems reasonable to them. And they birth the nations of the Moabites and Ammon.

--- Shall Not Enter into the Congregation
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 19:37
fig: Deuteronomy 23:3-4 | Deuteronomy 23:3-4
callout: Remember, the law given the Israelites would prohibit Moabites from the assembly of God, **as a punishment for their maltreatment of the children of Israel and for engaging Balaam to curse the children of Israel**, while they journeyed in the wilderness. Just as the Lord says in Genesis 18 that faithful Abraham and his descendants will keep the faith of God, backslidden Lot's won't. [[Genesis 18:19]]

--- So Many Lessons
center: There's so many lessons to take from this for saved believers living in this wicked world.
